title: tag:query
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Insert a tag filter in the simplified query and search

`tag:query <tag|negative_tag|mixed_tag> <tag>` asks which field of the tag model to search ([[Hierarchical tags]]) and a tag, completing over the paths of the existing ones (a tag under several parents is offered by each), then adds `<field> -> (path =>* "<tag>")` — the tag of that path, and those under it — to the normal DSL field of the metarecord list and runs the search; the focus stays where it was. With `negative_tag` it finds the records that deny the tag or one under it. The filter is AND-ed with what the field holds, a query with a top-level `OR` being parenthesized first. A filter the query already holds, as a term of its top-level `AND` and in this spelling, is not added again, and nothing runs. <<cmd "tag:unquery">> takes it back off.

The command writes the query the list last applied: what was typed in its two fields and not applied is replaced, as with any command that shows a query ([[Why the two query fields are AND-ed]]). A later command that shows a query replaces the normal DSL, and the filters with it. The keys are `, q`, `, - q` and `, = q` ([[Tagging from the GUI]]). Written in the shipped `commands.js`, where its questions and what it runs can be edited ([[User commands]]).
